{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.835323Z","id":"9af25a7800d328f862b2b6ab15b464b9df4a9d480e1aa4459bee94116ed620d2","body":{"detail":"path p export codex|pi|copilot records the caller's cwd (std::env::current_dir) as the session's instead of the source session's; the hermetic tool ran from / and this constant stands in for that. When the export is fixed to carry the source cwd, known_defects@claude.snap changes (written_cwd becomes the source cwd) and this constant becomes unused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"The pipeline hands codex, pi and copilot projectors the hermetic caller cwd `/`, which is what a fixed caller-cwd defect would stop writing","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.846593Z","id":"2a4e07671b0f5bf4860a70cbf11abaa0b0eba48650bdcc83d254467fe141f52d","body":{"detail":"The other three agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, drop the canonical form here so the golden is the real bytes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.856774Z","id":"8cb0124a31291ac6b5706d40348239520356a7341a7ba8604e38ff84b8e6ced9","body":{"detail":"round_trip@copilot@claude.snap is now 'compared' where goldens/roundtrip/copilot-claude.json pinned an error from the hermetic placement step (fixture lacks the session identity claude needs). The Unreadable variant stays for a future pair that genuinely cannot be re-read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"b7b8e0322b119b1e986444e6d40af469ad399cce43b194183a3e3a07d276fb11"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:31:12.866880Z","id":"e185bc72fd107804a11a04224fadc4672443192143435772c4cf6f53c3bc8a3a","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. Resolve this record when a defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Three defects pinned as expected current behaviour; a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755754Z","id":"90e64df3125f4d1524949c2e13fb9e19b7c31d40018941fb8df9a61d419d8298","body":{"detail":"path p export codex|pi|copilot records the caller's cwd (std::env::current_dir) as the session's instead of the source session's, and export gemini bakes the caller's directory into projectHash and directories; the hermetic tool ran from / and this constant stands in for that. When the export is fixed to carry the source cwd, known_defects@claude.snap changes (written_cwd becomes the source cwd), every gemini projection's projectHash/directories change, and this constant becomes unused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"The pipeline hands codex, pi, copilot and gemini projectors the hermetic caller cwd `/`, which is what a fixed caller-cwd defect would stop writing","supersedes":"9af25a7800d328f862b2b6ab15b464b9df4a9d480e1aa4459bee94116ed620d2","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755856Z","id":"8d60a30c9a0aba4773d9ea2f561da147417de6323537a02d8275de9cd848c920","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"2a4e07671b0f5bf4860a70cbf11abaa0b0eba48650bdcc83d254467fe141f52d","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755920Z","id":"207c648136a27f9351d94a4c4db84a28d8b042d46b7662455c404a2467d20101","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":508},"end":{"line":508},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"8cb0124a31291ac6b5706d40348239520356a7341a7ba8604e38ff84b8e6ced9","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.755974Z","id":"2ac0a1e747def033b9a72aa0296d25d88184ef7c48ef1f5456f2fedb42f0fa00","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. An accounting defect that goes to an empty mismatches list is fixed: accept the snapshot, delete the Defect, and the invariant in tests/goldens.rs tightens by itself. Resolve this record when every defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Six defects pinned as expected current behaviour (three of them accounting gaps that also exempt their set from the accounting invariant); a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","supersedes":"e185bc72fd107804a11a04224fadc4672443192143435772c4cf6f53c3bc8a3a","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756085Z","id":"0b188981a320abccdc1fe377e1ef33b8719cb53679fb2d9ead78c61dd4b426ed","body":{"detail":"When the adapter learns the stream (header line, message lines with `type`, `$set`-style mutations without), replace this with its reader so `read` for Gemini is the adapter's own path for both shapes. Until then `path p derive gemini` cannot read a session Gemini 0.47 wrote, which the gemini golden proves only in-process.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":295},"content_hash":"c3ff8b01e48dbc692c778663e859492367b6fa47184ea4a7e89130426e557f36"},"summary":"The goldens crate assembles Gemini 0.47's JSONL chat stream itself because toolpath_gemini::ConversationReader reads one JSON document only; this is the third copy of that assembly (toolpath-gemini/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs, path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs)","tags":["goldens","gemini","duplication","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756118Z","id":"9cab016c6cb69f9e3bfbbfd32ae7c6cbb861a2784210064ffb51490828c0b46d","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/validate.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756157Z","id":"550eecc82d68305778af78eee98aca3ea199a33d3a8952113c6bf5c10d380821","body":{"detail":"path-cli's lib.rs declares `mod schema` privately and BUNDLED_KINDS likewise, so the goldens crate includes the kind schema files by relative path. Making the module pub (or moving validation next to toolpath::SCHEMA_JSON) would leave one validator; until then a change to path-cli's validation must be mirrored here or validate@<set> stops meaning `path p validate`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"2e76458dc44fc17b7b7690bd49954bdffe4e8760b1e602e2b68a2b282fa2d752"},"summary":"Reimplements path-cli's private `schema` module (base toolpath.schema.json plus the bundled kind schemas by meta.kind) over the same embedded bytes","tags":["goldens","duplication","schema","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/accounting.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:49:41.756199Z","id":"18549e27eaac75e08112044300f95ae714dcd48327d0c2821f85050a3bc987cf","body":{"detail":"The fixes live in the adapter crates: toolpath_gemini::provider::sum_usage and toolpath_opencode::provider::accumulate_total must add breakdowns class by class as toolpath_convo::extract does since c65a6b6; copilot needs session-level totals carried into the document (derive writes no total_usage) or per-turn input/cache attribution.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"ede19ac64e35ab5434e8e316e60bc7478b77e2c38087c8628f81be6507ca3da1"},"summary":"The accounting contract holds for claude, claude-session, claude-compacted, codex, pi and cursor and is broken for copilot (session totals only on session.shutdown), gemini and opencode (sum_usage/accumulate_total drop per-turn breakdowns); the three gaps are pinned in defects.rs","tags":["goldens","accounting","known-defect","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:55.799041Z","id":"c62500a0424141c0245c783c7fb7344dea0c045c097071b3eb279373cc61dea7","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":481},"end":{"line":481},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"207c648136a27f9351d94a4c4db84a28d8b042d46b7662455c404a2467d20101","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:55.799161Z","id":"2fd56e2601b246b0cd173b564877b9690b12b6b4f924a3f8a9b9c157abcb76dd","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":292},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","supersedes":"9cab016c6cb69f9e3bfbbfd32ae7c6cbb861a2784210064ffb51490828c0b46d","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:55.817235Z","id":"48316e5455f9661818809fc6564b6f6e18dffb4edc2441f11516c011c5ab0ac9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Fixed: toolpath_gemini::ConversationReader reads the 0.47 record stream (upsert by id, $set, $rewindTo); the pipeline, cross_harness_matrix and real_fixture_roundtrip all call it","supersedes":"0b188981a320abccdc1fe377e1ef33b8719cb53679fb2d9ead78c61dd4b426ed","tags":["session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","reason:fixed"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:21:48.240684Z","id":"1bca87fd8af4880a2661d3ab9fc2324f35984821b17ff4a18a0ff4139ce104a5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","supersedes":"90e64df3125f4d1524949c2e13fb9e19b7c31d40018941fb8df9a61d419d8298","tags":["known-defect","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","reason:invalid"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:21:48.259994Z","id":"b839958fe42d822f01f5667e1e873da8cce97aa34e4f89fbb635e4e6bb7133c5","body":{"detail":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"CALLER_CWD is the directory a projection is resumed in, not a stand-in for a defect: the caller's cwd is the contract for codex, pi, copilot and gemini","tags":["goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:21:58.510877Z","id":"122da212472671c8e0d215332a5fda04abd602a91ace0a60d6cc56bd40efe017","body":{"detail":"The old tool's judge functions (Fixed vs Worse) classified a changed body; here the classification is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. An accounting defect that goes to an empty mismatches list is fixed: accept the snapshot, delete the Defect, and the invariant in tests/goldens.rs tightens by itself. Resolve this record when every defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted. claude-to-codex-caller-cwd was retired 2026-10-19 as not a defect (pr/22): a pin's reference value is itself a claim to check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Five defects pinned as expected current behaviour (three of them accounting gaps that also exempt their set from the accounting invariant); a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","supersedes":"2ac0a1e747def033b9a72aa0296d25d88184ef7c48ef1f5456f2fedb42f0fa00","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:56:32.678152Z","id":"cf4e2d360d37040594dddc82c2217bc51f4a62bec0651d7db679168935f12d90","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":496},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"c62500a0424141c0245c783c7fb7344dea0c045c097071b3eb279373cc61dea7","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/accounting.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:23:30.321367Z","id":"19b5a82642c37f773ecb7ee78a878b92481f2d53c723459c3a70538519cf453d","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Fixed: gemini sum_usage and opencode accumulate_total add breakdowns class by class; copilot puts every counter only session.shutdown reports, verbatim, on the last assistant turn, so the steps sum to the session total. The accounting contract holds for every set and no known defect pins a gap","supersedes":"18549e27eaac75e08112044300f95ae714dcd48327d0c2821f85050a3bc987cf","tags":["session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","reason:fixed"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:08:54.811658Z","id":"d1465c82ea302bedcaf167c2048b4c3974bc35f881e7c42490f2f96b8fbd6f3c","body":{"detail":"The classification of a changed known_defects body is the reviewer's, guided by tests/goldens.rs's doc comment. claude-to-codex-caller-cwd was retired 2026-10-19 as not a defect (pr/22-codex-resume-cwd). The three accounting defects (gemini and opencode totals dropping breakdowns, copilot session totals on no step) were fixed in their adapters the same day (pr/*-accounting-totals) and their Defect entries deleted, with the accounting_gap measure and Target::Document they alone used; a new accounting defect brings both back. Resolve this record when every defect is fixed and its snapshot accepted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"2e1040b296bb70b5e4614fe3f886af2ddb83174dab983c22fda92737fc98ffe0"},"summary":"Two defects pinned as expected current behaviour (codex-to-claude-illegal-types, claude-roundtrip-renames), neither an accounting gap: the accounting invariant holds for every set; a diff in known_defects@<set>.snap is FIXED or WORSE and must be read, insta cannot tell the two apart","supersedes":"122da212472671c8e0d215332a5fda04abd602a91ace0a60d6cc56bd40efe017","tags":["goldens","known-defect","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:21:50.495071Z","id":"0c8cb0692057add3165a95a2ecba4605a0a24494d2e98ea6af99c1ce81765919","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Every defect is fixed: codex-to-claude-illegal-types and claude-roundtrip-renames fixed in toolpath-claude (pr/28), the accounting three in pr/27; DEFECTS is empty and known_defects@<set>.snap is [] for every set","supersedes":"d1465c82ea302bedcaf167c2048b4c3974bc35f881e7c42490f2f96b8fbd6f3c","tags":["goldens","known-defect","reason:fixed","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:36:28.681029Z","id":"526d3a25a88af2522546bf61d6230665aad73c4ad1fb82df1cd21e829d118d6c","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":506},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"cf4e2d360d37040594dddc82c2217bc51f4a62bec0651d7db679168935f12d90","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:01:06.844482Z","id":"6c8a2e928b72b113a2fdf76cf4bf050613d257da64221423d52c9d3f7da42c3a","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"8d60a30c9a0aba4773d9ea2f561da147417de6323537a02d8275de9cd848c920","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:01:06.844607Z","id":"1ed3cef0bf59d394fde4ae0e8ff308b05f59b10adc79f8b2738b6b78b2aaad88","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","supersedes":"2fd56e2601b246b0cd173b564877b9690b12b6b4f924a3f8a9b9c157abcb76dd","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:01:06.844920Z","id":"2ab7d3eadd1d77ab6800807715c314eefa5042fa785b672dc45ada66cf316667","body":{"detail":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"CALLER_CWD is the directory a projection is resumed in, not a stand-in for a defect: the caller's cwd is the contract for codex, pi, copilot and gemini","supersedes":"b839958fe42d822f01f5667e1e873da8cce97aa34e4f89fbb635e4e6bb7133c5","tags":["goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:01:06.846375Z","id":"beccf27a693360a690f29582cb171406fccfdb93db45c3a5fe98b0864374d651","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":515},"end":{"line":515},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"cf4e2d360d37040594dddc82c2217bc51f4a62bec0651d7db679168935f12d90","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
