{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:49:26.184366Z","id":"47310d3f314a60bba43dc5aef995ddc6bdadb6ba48fa75d1ec1e0fb445c96fc8","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":341},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","supersedes":"0d022915b3a3d0a1a35bbc09798295af09631aed1c6888559c49c0c7259b8354","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:49:26.242025Z","id":"f8cea86a68f25837bed5b2abb3c04d8608fdbbc2447a44beaf566abf8297654f","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":593},"end":{"line":593},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"c9e19e1babef8e3a0d85dd27a799216939ec72535e3f7c2c016d50ac9b995bb2","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T19:08:07.498281Z","id":"0d487e12fbf96d41f05b36bab2a3ac94a62f0f2df52469f9d0d082acdac8edfa","body":{"detail":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"CALLER_CWD is the directory a projection is resumed in, not a stand-in for a defect: the caller's cwd is the contract for codex, pi, copilot and gemini","supersedes":"98ef9cbd37b7cc86dbbbba1ab5969dda5ff3c2db9956c86b6664bf989d8390aa","tags":["goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T19:08:07.563120Z","id":"57a5a8b83e8ba133550059550f098b830d769c5fd0a785d0d0771d6fbb22a0c0","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"bae67ed2481f42d62209eeb476767341fac23b908bcd76209138ced8178e6ee8","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T19:08:07.628223Z","id":"dd6fa6f81587aad09aa3a348ba38b13c47fb63c43dfd2c699705b2e9a477282e","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":344},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","supersedes":"47310d3f314a60bba43dc5aef995ddc6bdadb6ba48fa75d1ec1e0fb445c96fc8","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
